                <pb facs="0596" n="484" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg484"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/13322: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Second Secretary of Embassy in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Atcheson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-12-12T12:00:00+08:00">December 12,
                        1935—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received December 12—9:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>136. The Central Executive Committee this morning names the following “Cabinet”
                    Ministers: <list>
                        <item>Interior, Chiang Tso-pin;</item>
                        <item>Foreign Affairs, Chang Chun;</item>
                        <item>Military Administration, Ho Ying-chin;</item>
                        <item>Navy, Chen Shao-kuan;</item>
                        <item>Finance, H. H. Kung;</item>
                        <item>Industries, Wu Ting-chang;</item>
                        <item>Communications, Ku Meng-yu;</item>
                        <item>Education, Wang Shih-chieh;</item>
                        <item>Railways, Chang Kia-ngau (Chang Kung-chuan).</item>
                    </list></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Atcheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
